{
 "_doc": [
  "The v7.0 catalogue's OWN sub-vertical applicability, lifted from",
  "`2_Capability_Map!Tier` in the four Pillar workbooks at",
  "gs://digital-maturity-assessor-catalogue-staging/v7.0/ on 2026-08-15.",
  "",
  "Why it is here. `variant_subvertical()` derives a cell's owner from its id",
  "suffix, which is the catalogue's minting convention rather than a stated",
  "fact. That derivation is now CHECKED against the catalogue's own column:",
  "",
  "  T1        686 cells  a base cell; applies to every sub-vertical",
  "  T2-<CODE> 127 cells  the catalogue NAMES the owner",
  "  T2         38 cells  a variant the catalogue leaves unqualified",
  "",
  "Measured: on all 127 where the catalogue names an owner, the id suffix",
  "agrees. Zero contradictions. On the 38 it leaves bare, the suffix does name",
  "one \u2014 and those include P1C1.3.IC1 'Insurance Line Strategy' and",
  "P1C1.4.IB1, two of the exact cells a credit union was served in the defect",
  "this module exists to close. So the suffix rule is not merely consistent",
  "with the catalogue, it is strictly more complete than it, and replacing it",
  "with the column would LOSE 38 exclusions.",
  "",
  "This file exists so that stops being an assumption. If a later catalogue",
  "version qualifies the remaining 38, or contradicts the suffix anywhere,",
  "test_variant_owner_matches_the_catalogue fails and the rule is re-derived",
  "rather than quietly drifting from its own source of truth.",
  "",
  "Taxonomy, not client data: these are catalogue cell ids and their tier."
 ],
